WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.233 --> 00:00:18.175
Just then Alpha began ringing.

2
00:00:18.195 --> 00:00:21.057
"Shh," Ally said.

3
00:00:21.077 --> 00:00:22.518
"I'm trying to think!"

4
00:00:23.238 --> 00:00:25.360
"Illogical response," Alpha said.

5
00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:26.821
"You have a phone call."

6
00:00:26.841 --> 00:00:30.283
"Oh!" Ally pushed the talk button.

7
00:00:30.303 --> 00:00:34.281
"Hello?" Mateo huffed on the other end.

8
00:00:35.361 --> 00:00:36.822
"Mateo, are you all right?"

9
00:00:36.842 --> 00:00:41.105
"Yes," Mateo replied breathlessly.

10
00:00:41.125 --> 00:00:44.927
"I tried to follow the limo on my bike, but I lost it.

11
00:00:45.827 --> 00:00:46.527
Are you all right?"

12
00:00:46.547 --> 00:00:48.228
"Not really!"

13
00:00:48.849 --> 00:00:50.249
Ally explained everything.

14
00:00:50.269 --> 00:00:52.190
"Don't worry.

15
00:00:52.691 --> 00:00:55.812
I'll get the meld medallion back from her," Mateo said.

16
00:00:56.293 --> 00:00:57.874
"Have Alpha send me your location.

17
00:00:58.294 --> 00:01:00.115
I'll be there as fast as I can!"

18
00:01:00.775 --> 00:01:05.861
While Ally waited for Mateo, she crept out of the bathroom to check out the P.O.D.'s technology.

19
00:01:07.362 --> 00:01:09.203
"Nothing here looks super advanced."

20
00:01:09.863 --> 00:01:12.104
Ally inspected the P.O.D.'s control panel.

21
00:01:12.124 --> 00:01:16.586
"Carparians are known to be exceptional engineers.

22
00:01:17.146 --> 00:01:18.907
Maybe Lainie is human after all.

23
00:01:19.487 --> 00:01:23.389
Still, I can't be sure until I see her with the meld medallion on."

24
00:01:23.849 --> 00:01:25.189
Ally finished her inspection.

25
00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:30.612
She'd just returned to the bathroom when someone burst into the P.O.D.

26
00:01:31.604 --> 00:01:32.284
"I'm here!"

27
00:01:32.745 --> 00:01:33.505
Mateo cried.

28
00:01:33.525 --> 00:01:36.766
"I've got good news and bad news.

29
00:01:37.247 --> 00:01:38.427
Which do you want first?"

30
00:01:39.227 --> 00:01:40.688
Ally stepped out of the bathroom.

31
00:01:40.708 --> 00:01:42.509
"The good news!"

32
00:01:43.649 --> 00:01:44.770
"Here's your medallion!"

33
00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:45.870
Mateo said.

34
00:01:50.773 --> 00:01:52.173
was wearing it when I got here.

35
00:01:52.593 --> 00:01:55.395
She looked like herself, not a Carparian.

36
00:01:55.875 --> 00:02:00.977
And she was so distracted by angry bird-watchers, she barely paid attention when I asked her if I

37
00:02:00.997 --> 00:02:02.957
could look at her unusual necklace."

38
00:02:06.078 --> 00:02:08.299
"Phew!" Ally slipped it on.

39
00:02:09.019 --> 00:02:10.179
"Angry bird-watchers?

40
00:02:10.579 --> 00:02:12.340
I thought they were reporters out there."

41
00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:16.101
"That's the bad news," Mateo replied.

42
00:02:16.121 --> 00:02:19.222
"Those bird-watchers found the whoopers' nest."

43
00:02:19.242 --> 00:02:21.722
"Huh? Why is that bad news?"

44
00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:25.163
"You'd better come with me."

45
00:02:26.123 --> 00:02:27.944
Mateo led Ally out of the P.O.D.

46
00:02:28.688 --> 00:02:31.850
As he'd said, Lainie was surrounded by bird-watchers.

47
00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:35.113
"Why are they so angry?"

48
00:02:35.513 --> 00:02:36.113
Ally asked.

49
00:02:36.654 --> 00:02:38.955
Mateo pointed to the top of the P.O.D.

50
00:02:38.975 --> 00:02:41.757
"The whoopers' nest is up there!"

51
00:02:43.539 --> 00:02:44.239
Ally gasped.

52
00:02:44.259 --> 00:02:47.381
"They're just birds!"

53
00:02:47.902 --> 00:02:48.482
Lainie said.

54
00:02:48.502 --> 00:02:52.044
"They could be the last whoopers in the world!"

55
00:02:52.445 --> 00:02:53.826
a bird-watcher shouted back.

56
00:02:53.846 --> 00:02:59.346
"If they don't successfully hatch these eggs, the species could go extinct."

57
00:02:59.366 --> 00:03:06.191
"Well, then I'll build a statue to their memory," Lainie said.

58
00:03:08.112 --> 00:03:10.414
That made the bird-watchers even angrier.

59
00:03:11.855 --> 00:03:12.756
Ally hurried over.

60
00:03:12.776 --> 00:03:14.537
"Now, now, everyone.

61
00:03:14.997 --> 00:03:17.179
I know we can resolve this peacefully.

62
00:03:17.759 --> 00:03:19.861
Bird-watchers, what do you want?"

63
00:03:19.881 --> 00:03:23.644
"That nest can't be moved," one said.

64
00:03:24.212 --> 00:03:28.955
"We want Lainie to delay the flight until the eggs have hatched, and the babies are big enough

65
00:03:28.995 --> 00:03:30.076
to leave the nest."

66
00:03:30.096 --> 00:03:33.499
"But that will take three months!"

67
00:03:34.059 --> 00:03:34.739
Lainie moaned.

68
00:03:39.363 --> 00:03:40.223
Ally turned to her.

69
00:03:40.243 --> 00:03:46.728
"There's no point in exploring other planets if we don't do everything we can to save the planet

70
00:03:46.788 --> 00:03:47.568
we're on."

71
00:03:48.629 --> 00:03:49.870
The bird-watchers cheered.

72
00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:51.231
"She's right!"

73
00:03:51.671 --> 00:03:52.452
"Listen to her!"

74
00:03:54.868 --> 00:03:55.608
Lainie sighed.

75
00:03:55.628 --> 00:04:00.931
"Fine. We should help the birds.

76
00:04:01.551 --> 00:04:02.912
I'll delay the launch."

77
00:04:05.173 --> 00:04:06.814
The bird-watchers cheered louder.

78
00:04:14.518 --> 00:04:18.980
I'll see you in three months, Ally," Lainie said as she started back to her limo.

79
00:04:21.696 --> 00:04:25.258
"And let me know if you ever want to sell that necklace."

80
00:04:26.519 --> 00:04:28.320
Ally nodded and waved good-bye.

81
00:04:33.363 --> 00:04:34.683
Ally," Mateo said.

82
00:04:34.703 --> 00:04:36.524
"That was really kind of you.

83
00:04:37.705 --> 00:04:41.207
You could have gone home, but you chose to save the whoopers."

84
00:04:42.348 --> 00:04:42.928
Ally shrugged.

85
00:04:42.948 --> 00:04:44.969
"I can wait three months.

86
00:04:45.929 --> 00:04:50.132
This way I'll have more time to convince your mom to stay in Sandville."

87
00:04:50.952 --> 00:04:51.752
Mateo grinned.

88
00:04:51.772 --> 00:04:53.553
"Sounds good to me!"

89
00:04:56.515 --> 00:05:00.056
But when they got back to Ray's house, Dawn's suitcases were gone.

90
00:05:00.076 --> 00:05:02.957
"I've failed!"

91
00:05:04.178 --> 00:05:04.798
Ally moaned.

92
00:05:05.158 --> 00:05:07.439
She sat on the couch, her head in her hands.

93
00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:13.642
Mateo looked miserable too, until a minute later, when Ray and Dawn walked in, laughing.

94
00:05:15.523 --> 00:05:18.044
"I'm glad you're here, Mateo," Dawn said.

95
00:05:18.888 --> 00:05:21.750
"I wanted to tell you that I've decided to go back to the city.

96
00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:24.231
You and your dad will stay here."

97
00:05:24.251 --> 00:05:28.413
"I don't understand," Ally burst out.

98
00:05:28.433 --> 00:05:32.115
"If you love each other, then why not stay together?

99
00:05:32.856 --> 00:05:35.757
Opening a shop here is the perfect solution!"

100
00:05:35.777 --> 00:05:39.579
"Things aren't always that simple," Dawn said.

101
00:05:39.599 --> 00:05:43.201
"We love each other, but we want different things.

102
00:05:44.002 --> 00:05:48.244
I want to be in the city for my career, and Ray's life is here with the diner.

103
00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:53.001
Mateo, you are the most important thing to us.

104
00:05:54.021 --> 00:05:57.762
Even when we aren't together, we will always be a family."

105
00:06:00.843 --> 00:06:02.863
Ally watched Mateo hug his parents.

106
00:06:03.504 --> 00:06:04.864
Then Ray reached for her.

107
00:06:04.884 --> 00:06:07.445
"You're part of our family too, Ally."

108
00:06:12.086 --> 00:06:16.367
guess there are all kinds of families," she thought, hugging all of them.

109
00:06:16.387 --> 00:06:19.408
"And families don't all have to look the same."

110
00:06:20.101 --> 00:06:27.095
After all, her parents were her Astralian family, and Ray and Mateo were her Earth family—at least for

111
00:06:27.176 --> 00:06:27.957
three more months!
